  "one_candidate": {
    "mechanism": "Native SpawnGroupData shares first tropical fish appearance and leader; free-variant branch ends the current inner spawn group after an add request.",
    "steps": [
      "NaturalSpawner resets SpawnGroupData to null for each outer group attempt. After local selection, placement, collision and position acceptance, finalizeSpawn receives the previous return value with NATURAL provenance, before any world-add request.",
      "AbstractSchoolingFish initializes plain group data with the first instance as leader. With existing group data it attaches the new fish to that leader and increments the leader instance school size before the world-add request.",
      "TropicalFish after super preserves an existing TropicalFishGroupData variant with no new selection draw. First fish with a draw less than 0.9D chooses a common palette-pattern tuple and replaces plain group data with the same leader and chosen variant. That value is reused on later members of the current native group.",
      "The alternative first fish flips isSchool to false, independently chooses a pattern and two colors, and retains plain group data. Its isMaxGroupSizeReached returns true after its world-add request; this breaks the current inner group loop unless the enclosing Forge pack-size check already returned. It does not cancel the caller or every later separate group attempt. The independently drawn tuple can coincide with a common tuple.",
      "NaturalSpawner increments attempt counters, requests addFreshEntityWithPassengers and calls subsequent accounting before the pack and group-stop checks; wrapper discards individual addFreshEntity boolean results. Eight is the base table group bound and default pack size, not an observed school of eight. A rejected add does not by itself roll back group data or the follower-increment operation in the cited path.",
      "Packed Variant persists on the entity and is copied to or restored from the bucket numeric tag along the separate BUCKET branch. Initial leader linkage and isSchool are absent from the cited save writes. A later FollowFlockLeaderGoal uses same runtime class and follow state for nearby recruitment, without checking packed appearance or natural spawn reason."
    ],
    "dedup_accepted": [
